1
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,800
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,724 --> 00:00:45,964
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,091 --> 00:00:48,317
=Episode 21=

4
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:07,640
(Guizhen Cottage)

5
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:09,640
You tyrant! Pay for my family's deaths!

6
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:10,480
Pay for my family's deaths!

7
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,719
Pay for my family's deaths!

8
00:01:12,079 --> 00:01:12,640
(Shouhe.)

9
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,359
(Today, he'll see for himself)

10
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:17,959
(what Guizhen Cottage really is.)

11
00:01:19,599 --> 00:01:20,159
Hurry! Hurry!

12
00:01:20,159 --> 00:01:21,159
Pay for my family's deaths!

13
00:01:21,159 --> 00:01:21,519
Move!

14
00:01:21,519 --> 00:01:23,120
My father entered the work site alive.

15
00:01:23,359 --> 00:01:25,000
All that was left of him was ash!

16
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:25,400
Smash it!

17
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:26,959
What plague burns people alive?

18
00:01:27,239 --> 00:01:27,879
You tyrant!

19
00:01:28,079 --> 00:01:28,920
Give me justice!

20
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:30,079
Smash everything!

21
00:01:31,719 --> 00:01:32,319
Smash it all!

22
00:01:33,319 --> 00:01:34,239
Destroy it all!

23
00:01:36,079 --> 00:01:36,760
At noon,

24
00:01:36,959 --> 00:01:38,159
stick to the plan we agreed on.

25
00:01:38,159 --> 00:01:38,599
All right.

26
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:40,400
The bigger the commotion, the better.

27
00:01:40,599 --> 00:01:41,159
Understood?

28
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:49,599
Your Majesty!

29
00:01:50,719 --> 00:01:51,200
Your Majesty!

30
00:01:51,719 --> 00:01:52,400
Something's happened.

31
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:53,760
Outside the cottage,

32
00:01:54,159 --> 00:01:55,599
a crowd of protesters has gathered.

33
00:01:55,599 --> 00:01:55,920
They say...

34
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:57,879
they want justice.

35
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:00,439
Justice?

36
00:02:04,799 --> 00:02:05,480
They say

37
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,680
when the cottage was being built,

38
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,040
hundreds of laborers were conscripted.

39
00:02:09,239 --> 00:02:11,959
Shen You had Noble Consort Chen
and Zhang Heng behind him.

40
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:13,319
He withheld their wages,

41
00:02:13,319 --> 00:02:14,280
and abused the workers,

42
00:02:14,879 --> 00:02:17,080
so the workers grew weak and fell ill.

43
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,400
Then, to cover it up,

44
00:02:19,199 --> 00:02:20,840
he had them burned alive.

45
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,280
They also say

46
00:02:23,759 --> 00:02:24,560
the free clinic

47
00:02:25,199 --> 00:02:27,400
is all just for show.

48
00:02:28,039 --> 00:02:29,000
They say this cottage

49
00:02:29,439 --> 00:02:31,360
wasn't the late Empress's charity,

50
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:32,479
but rather...

51
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:35,520
a graveyard for the people.

52
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:36,000
How dare they!

53
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:36,479
But...

54
00:02:36,639 --> 00:02:38,479
Guizhen Cottage was
Roujia's life's work.

55
00:02:38,759 --> 00:02:40,120
I give medicine here daily to help them.

56
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:42,080
Yet they call me a hypocrite?

57
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:44,280
Please calm down, Your Majesty.

58
00:02:44,719 --> 00:02:45,080
There's...

59
00:02:45,319 --> 00:02:46,560
one more thing.

60
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:48,639
Concubine Hui

61
00:02:48,919 --> 00:02:50,919
saw the crowd growing

62
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:52,120
and went to calm them.

63
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:53,319
But then...

64
00:02:53,599 --> 00:02:54,759
the crowd grew violent.

65
00:02:54,919 --> 00:02:55,560
In the chaos,

66
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:56,960
someone pulled a knife

67
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:58,800
and stabbed Her Highness.

68
00:02:59,000 --> 00:02:59,680
What?

69
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:01,520
Su!

70
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:03,439
Your Majesty! Your Majesty!

71
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:14,759
Su.

72
00:03:17,439 --> 00:03:18,560
Su, you're awake.

73
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:24,599
I'm right here, aren't I?

74
00:03:25,319 --> 00:03:26,080
Che.

75
00:03:26,759 --> 00:03:28,000
You look so worn out.

76
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,879
It hurts me to see you like this.

77
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:33,479
That stab wound...

78
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:36,199
If it had gone a little deeper,

79
00:03:36,879 --> 00:03:38,240
I would've lost you.

80
00:03:39,159 --> 00:03:40,039
Do you know

81
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,360
I kept calling you,
but you wouldn't wake up.

82
00:03:42,719 --> 00:03:44,319
I kept calling you,
but you wouldn't wake up.

83
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:45,960
I once thought

84
00:03:46,599 --> 00:03:47,759
losing Roujia

85
00:03:50,159 --> 00:03:51,960
was the worst pain imaginable.

86
00:03:53,199 --> 00:03:54,840
But now I know

87
00:03:55,439 --> 00:03:56,800
if I lost you,

88
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:58,560
it would be even more unbearable.

89
00:03:59,879 --> 00:04:00,719
Promise me.

90
00:04:01,479 --> 00:04:02,919
Don't leave this world before I do,

91
00:04:03,919 --> 00:04:04,520
okay?

92
00:04:06,039 --> 00:04:06,840
Okay.

93
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,039
I promise.

94
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:10,680
This time,

95
00:04:11,639 --> 00:04:13,240
I failed to protect you.

96
00:04:13,479 --> 00:04:14,479
I've already issued a decree.

97
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:17,280
You're now Consort Hui.

98
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:19,960
I...

99
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:24,319
I'm deeply grateful, Your Majesty.

100
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,920
A consort's title is nothing.

101
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,839
We still have plenty of time.

102
00:04:29,639 --> 00:04:31,079
I'll give you everything you want

103
00:04:31,399 --> 00:04:32,399
to make up for it.

104
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:38,720
One stab wound,

105
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,519
and now she's a consort?

106
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,879
A mere village woman

107
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:45,160
is fit to stand as my equal?

108
00:04:45,439 --> 00:04:46,319
Please calm down, Your Highness.

109
00:04:46,959 --> 00:04:48,040
More importantly,

110
00:04:48,399 --> 00:04:49,959
after yesterday's riot,

111
00:04:50,399 --> 00:04:52,439
His Majesty knows about
the corruption in the cottage.

112
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:54,319
If he investigates further,

113
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,600
it could implicate you.

114
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:59,439
What was my uncle thinking?

115
00:04:59,959 --> 00:05:01,480
He couldn't even kill off
a few commoners?

116
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,360
He let them live long enough

117
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,079
to ruin my plans?

118
00:05:05,399 --> 00:05:07,040
Vice Director Shen does have a plan.

119
00:05:07,879 --> 00:05:09,120
He just sent word.

120
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:10,920
He's captured someone

121
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:13,879
who often met with Consort Hui
in secret at her stall.

122
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,639
They must know who she really is.

123
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:17,160
Mm.

124
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:25,680
Su.

125
00:05:26,399 --> 00:05:27,680
Those rioters from yesterday

126
00:05:27,959 --> 00:05:29,360
are all in the imperial prison.

127
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:30,439
I won't spare them.

128
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:31,199
Your Majesty.

129
00:05:31,759 --> 00:05:33,720
They were just acting
in the heat of anger.

130
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:35,279
If you punish them severely,

131
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,680
it'll only look like the imperial family
is trying to silence them.

132
00:05:38,639 --> 00:05:40,079
I beg Your Majesty

133
00:05:40,319 --> 00:05:41,639
to investigate this thoroughly.

134
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:44,120
Not just to get justice for me,

135
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:46,360
but to clear the imperial family's name.

136
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,279
All right.

137
00:05:48,959 --> 00:05:49,759
I promise.

138
00:05:51,839 --> 00:05:52,639
Your Majesty.

139
00:05:53,759 --> 00:05:54,399
Your Majesty.

140
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:56,319
Consort Chen requests an audience.

141
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:01,720
Isn't she confined to her quarters?

142
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:02,959
Who let her out?

143
00:06:03,399 --> 00:06:04,040
Your Majesty.

144
00:06:04,759 --> 00:06:05,959
Consort Chen says

145
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:08,560
Consort Hui hid her true identity

146
00:06:08,879 --> 00:06:09,879
and deceived Your Majesty.

147
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:12,000
She also brought a witness.

148
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:19,040
Let her in.

149
00:06:19,839 --> 00:06:20,519
Send her in.

150
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:27,800
Your Majesty.

151
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,040
What trouble are you here to cause now?

152
00:06:37,639 --> 00:06:38,600
I wouldn't dare.

153
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:39,920
I only...

154
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:41,519
can't bear to see Your Majesty

155
00:06:41,519 --> 00:06:42,759
deceived any longer.

156
00:06:43,399 --> 00:06:43,959
Your Majesty.

157
00:06:44,199 --> 00:06:45,480
Do you remember, three years ago,

158
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:47,199
the grass weaver who died in the palace,

159
00:06:47,199 --> 00:06:48,199
Chen Shouhe?

160
00:06:48,839 --> 00:06:50,759
I had Jiyun Pavilion searched.

161
00:06:51,199 --> 00:06:52,399
And in Consort Hui's quarters,

162
00:06:52,399 --> 00:06:53,240
we actually found this.

163
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:58,079
This woven grass ring

164
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:00,680
uses the exact same weave
Chen Shouhe used.

165
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,319
And there's more.

166
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:03,720
Consort Hui

167
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:05,720
appeared out of nowhere three years ago.

168
00:07:06,319 --> 00:07:07,319
Before then,

169
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:08,879
official household records

170
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,120
and village registries

171
00:07:10,439 --> 00:07:11,839
contained no trace of her.

172
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,160
Because...

173
00:07:14,879 --> 00:07:17,040
she isn't Su Cao at all.

174
00:07:17,480 --> 00:07:18,279
She is

175
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,399
Chen Shouhe's wife,

176
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:21,800
Su Wanniang.

177
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:42,667
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

178
00:07:42,801 --> 00:07:46,414
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

179
00:07:46,649 --> 00:07:49,248
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

180
00:07:49,285 --> 00:07:51,565
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

181
00:07:51,612 --> 00:07:55,441
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

182
00:07:55,843 --> 00:07:59,196
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

183
00:08:00,123 --> 00:08:03,636
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

184
00:08:04,136 --> 00:08:06,703
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

185
00:08:06,829 --> 00:08:08,862
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

186
00:08:08,929 --> 00:08:12,706
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

187
00:08:13,056 --> 00:08:17,389
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

188
00:08:17,612 --> 00:08:21,119
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

189
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:24,153
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

190
00:08:24,220 --> 00:08:29,834
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

191
00:08:29,874 --> 00:08:32,888
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

192
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:38,937
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

193
00:08:39,604 --> 00:08:46,559
♪The past has faded away♪

194
00:08:46,559 --> 00:08:50,591
♪The past has faded away♪
